# Overload — environment variables.
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) for local development. NEVER commit real secrets.
#
# Environment model (docs/technical/environment-isolation.md, OVE-111):
#   • LOCAL dev  → the Supabase CLI stack (`npx supabase start`, Docker).
#   • PREVIEW    → Vercel Preview deployments → the `overload-dev` Supabase
#                  project (synthetic data only). Set in Vercel's Preview scope.
#   • PRODUCTION → Vercel Production → `overload-prod` (ref ycxvdiklpefyhdclxyau).
# There is no staging tier. A Preview/Development deployment whose database or
# Supabase variables name the Production ref fails its build and refuses to start.
#
# WARNING: anything that reads `.env` (prisma CLI, `next dev`/`next build`, the
# operator scripts) uses whatever is here. Keep ONLY local-stack values in
# `.env` / `.env.local` — never hosted (dev or production) values, not even
# commented out. For a deliberate operator run against a hosted project, EXPORT
# DATABASE_URL, DIRECT_URL and NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL for that one project in
# the shell (exported values win over .env) and confirm it with --confirm-ref.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT — values for the `npx supabase start` stack.
# `supabase start` prints the Project URL, the DB URL, and two keys:
#   • "Publishable" (sb_publishable_…) → NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#   • "Secret"      (sb_secret_…)      → SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (import only)
# Re-print them any time with `npx supabase status -o env` (PUBLISHABLE_KEY and
# SECRET_KEY). Older CLIs call these the "anon" and "service_role" keys
# (ANON_KEY / SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, long eyJ… JWTs); either form works.
# The defaults below match a standard local stack (ports from
# supabase/config.toml).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Server-only (NEVER prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_). Local stack Postgres (port 54322).
# Local has no separate pooler, so DATABASE_URL and DIRECT_URL are the same.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres

# Public (safe to ship). Local API gateway + the local "Publishable" key printed
# by `npx supabase start` (a shared local default, not a secret).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<"Publishable" key (sb_publishable_…) from `npx supabase start`>

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVICE-ROLE ("Secret") KEY — server-only, NEVER prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Used by (1) the exercise catalog import (`npm run db:seed`) to write images to
# Storage, and (2) since Accounts (Pitch 9), the app's server-only auth-admin
# facade (src/lib/supabase/admin.ts) to create invite-gated accounts and delete
# an account's auth identity. It never touches application tables.
# Production: set it in Vercel (server env, Production only) by hand from the
# Accounts runbook; never in a file. Locally, set the stack's key in `.env`.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<"Secret" key (sb_secret_…) from `npx supabase start`>

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SIGNUP MODE — server-only, NEVER prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ (Public Accounts, R1).
# Tri-state door, read in exactly one place (src/lib/accounts/signup-gate.ts):
#   closed  — no form; "Signup isn't open".
#   invite  — an invite-code field appears first; a valid OVERLOAD_INVITE_CODE
#             is required (the owner's launch config).
#   public  — anyone may sign up, no code. Leave this OFF in production until
#             the launch-readiness checklist passes (a human step, never a run).
# Unset, or any other value, resolves to CLOSED (the production default and the
# rollout gate).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OVERLOAD_SIGNUP_MODE=invite
#
# Invite code for invite mode — server-only, NEVER prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Compared constant-time; surrounding spaces ignored. Unset means NO code is
# valid, so invite mode admits no one until it is set.
# OVERLOAD_INVITE_CODE=
#
# DEPRECATED alias, kept only for back-compat so a mid-migration environment
# never silently opens: honored ONLY when OVERLOAD_SIGNUP_MODE is unset, where
# "true" -> public and anything else -> closed. Prefer OVERLOAD_SIGNUP_MODE.
# OVERLOAD_SIGNUP_OPEN=true
#
# Exercise-library import target confirmation (OVE-111). A hosted project is
# refused unless it is confirmed by project REF: `npx tsx prisma/seed.ts
# --confirm-ref <ref>`, or this variable (a hostname is never accepted:
# Production and the dev project share the pooler host). The connected database
# must also carry the dev identity marker. Production additionally needs the
# explicit --production command-line flag; there is no variable form of that
# opt-in. Set this only on the command line, never in a file.
# OVERLOAD_IMPORT_CONFIRM_HOST and OVERLOAD_IMPORT_PRODUCTION are refused if set.
# OVERLOAD_IMPORT_CONFIRM_REF=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BOT CHALLENGE — Cloudflare Turnstile (Public Accounts, PA2 / R6).
# Server-enforced human check on signup (and, from PA4, forgot-password). The
# server ALWAYS verifies the token before any account work.
#   • NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY — PUBLIC widget key; safe to ship. When
#     unset, the widget is disabled and the form's primary button stays
#     disabled (D3) — the server rejects a tokenless submit anyway.
#   • TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY — SERVER-ONLY (never NEXT_PUBLIC_; on the
#     client-bundle forbidden scan). Used only by src/lib/accounts/turnstile.ts
#     for the siteverify call.
# In a NON-production env with TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY unset, verification falls
# back to a documented bypass (a present token is treated as verified) so the
# local stack and integration tests run without reaching Cloudflare. Production
# REQUIRES a real key and never offers a client-controllable skip.
# For local manual testing, Cloudflare publishes always-pass test keys:
#   site 1x00000000000000000000AA / secret 1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TURNSTILE DEVELOPMENT BYPASS — server-only, NEVER prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# TURNSTILE_DISABLED=true hides the widget on signup and forgot-password, skips
# server-side verification, and skips the global hourly signup cap, so a
# developer can sign up and create repeated test accounts without Cloudflare.
# Decided in ONE place: src/lib/accounts/turnstile-bypass.ts. It applies only
# when the value is exactly `true` AND the process is either
#   • local development (`next dev`, NODE_ENV=development, not on a Vercel
#     deployment), or
#   • Vercel Preview (VERCEL_ENV=preview; set it for the `staging` branch only).
# VERCEL_ENV=production refuses it whatever the flag says, as does any
# production-mode process outside Preview (`next start`) and any database or
# Supabase variable naming the Production project. Absent or `false` = Turnstile
# on. The per-IP throttle, closed/invite modes, field validation, reserved
# usernames, and the disposable-email blocklist all still apply.
# Login has no bot challenge, so it is unaffected. Never set this in Production.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TURNSTILE_DISABLED=true

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AUTH EMAIL — custom SMTP (Resend) for recovery & verification (Public
# Accounts, PA3 / spec §11, R3). NAMES ONLY here — no real domains or creds.
#
# Recovery and verification route through Supabase Auth's OWN templates over
# this SMTP provider; the app adds no `resend` SDK and sends no mail itself.
# These SMTP values are consumed by SUPABASE, not the Next.js app: locally via
# the [auth.email.smtp] block in supabase/config.toml (commented out by
# default — the CLI stack catches mail in Inbucket/Mailpit at
# http://127.0.0.1:54324, so NONE of these need to be set for local dev); in
# production via the Supabase dashboard (Auth → SMTP Settings), set by the
# owner from the Public Accounts runbook. They are SERVER-ONLY and must NEVER
# be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#   • SMTP_HOST   — e.g. smtp.resend.com
#   • SMTP_PORT   — e.g. 587
#   • SMTP_USER   — Resend: the literal "resend"
#   • SMTP_PASS   — Resend API key (secret)
#   • SMTP_SENDER — the AUTHENTICATION sender identity, e.g. no-reply@<auth domain>
# The verified sending domain and its DNS (SPF/DKIM/DMARC) are owner/runbook
# steps; no real domain is chosen here.
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
# SMTP_SENDER=no-reply@<auth domain placeholder>

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPPORT ADDRESS — PUBLIC by design (Public Accounts, PA3 / spec §11).
# The SUPPORT sender identity, distinct from the authentication identity above.
# Rendered as a mailto: target on /support (PA6); it is NOT a sending
# integration. Because it is meant to be seen, it MAY be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_
# and is allowed in the client bundle (read by src/lib/accounts/support-email.ts).
# When unset, the app shows a visible placeholder. The real support domain is a
# runbook step.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_OVERLOAD_SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@<support domain placeholder>

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MOBILE API — app config and version gate (Pitch 21c). Server-only, all
# optional; with none set every app version is served and maintenance is off.
#   • MOBILE_MIN_APP_VERSION    — MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH; older apps get 426
#                                 upgrade_required (default 0.0.0)
#   • MOBILE_LATEST_APP_VERSION — MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH shown to the app as the
#                                 newest build (default: the minimum)
#   • MOBILE_MAINTENANCE        — "true" tells the app to show its maintenance
#                                 screen; the API keeps serving (advisory)
# An invalid version falls back to the default (the variable name is logged).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MOBILE_MIN_APP_VERSION=0.0.0
# MOBILE_LATEST_APP_VERSION=0.0.0
# MOBILE_MAINTENANCE=false

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TESTS — throwaway LOCAL Postgres for integration tests, reset between tests.
# MUST NOT point at any Supabase database (local stack or prod). If unset, the
# integration harness provisions an embedded throwaway Postgres automatically.
# Tests NEVER fall back to DATABASE_URL.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://overload_test:overload_test@127.0.0.1:5433/overload_test
